# NewTOS native C toolchain — tracking policy.
#
# Each ported library (libc = mintlib, gemlib) vendors its PRISTINE source as a
# tarball; build-*.sh extracts it and overlays our edits (overlay/). The
# extracted tree, object files, and the archive are build artifacts and are NOT
# tracked — the tarball + overlay/ + build script + tests ARE. A clone builds
# with no external network.

# Extracted source trees + build artifacts (regenerable via build-*.sh).
/libc/mintlib/
/libc/build/
/libc/libc.a
/gemlib/gemlib-0.44.0/
/gemlib/build/
/gemlib/gemlib.a
**/*.o
*.NCP

# Vendored trees not yet ported (vendor as tarball+overlay when the port begins).
/cflib/
/apps/

# macOS junk that FAT round-trips create.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.fseventsd
.Trashes
